initiative a</description></item><item><title>Hackers Exploit N-able MailAssure Flaw While AI Agents Exploit MONAI Label Zero-Day</title><link>https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/hackers-exploit-n-able-mailassure-flaw.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">14a00d8221c4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 06:02:45 -0000</pubDate><category>untagged</category><description>The Hacker News: The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) on Monday added two flaws impacting N-able MailAssure and MONAI Label to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog, citing evidence of active exploitation. The critical vulnerabilities are listed below - CVE-2026-134624 (CVSS score: 9.3) - A server-side request forgery (SSRF) vulnerability in N-able MailAssure's LDAP</description></item><item><title>Linux patches can take weeks, and OpenAI and Cisco built Shirudo to help in the meantime</title><link>https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2026/11/24/cisco-openai-shirudo</link><guid isPermaLink="false">a2551d2a358a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 06:00:50 -0000</pubDate><category>untagged</category><description>Help Net Security: OpenAI and Cisco released Shirudo, an open-source tool that puts temporary protections on running Linux systems while their owners work on a patch. Shirudo is Japanese for &amp;#8220;shield,&amp;#8221; which is also what each protection is called: a small program that blocks the specific behavior a vulnerability depends on, with no restart needed. Testing and deploying a patch can still take days or weeks</description></item><item><title>Kate Bush and Grace Jones urge Australian government not to legalise AI ‘theft’</title><link>https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/24/kate-bush-grace-jones-australian-artists-copyright-law-ai</link><guid isPermaLink="false">c945b3d23771</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:58:15 -0000</pubDate><category>untagged</category><description>The Guardian Technology: Singers among 7,000 artists and creatives urging Labor